    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571065/research-officer-bilingual": {
      "title": "Research Officer, Bilingual",
      "description": "Research Officer, Bilingual Job No.: 571065 Work type: Fixed Term Fixed term until June 2027 Bundoora (Melbourne) Classification: Level A - Base salary from $84,205 + 17% superannuation Hybrid work model support About the position The Research Officer will support MindCare4Women, a national research program funded by the Australian Government Department of Health, Disability and Ageing focused on reducing dementia risk among women from culturally and linguistically diverse (CALD) communities. Working with the Principal Investigator, Project Manager and broader research team, the Research Officer will contribute to the development and delivery of high-quality research outputs, including manuscripts, conference abstracts and presentations. The position will have a particular focus on data management, cleaning and mixed-methods analysis, including qualitative and quantitative data, and will contribute to the interpretation and dissemination of research findings. The successful candidate will be fluent in either Hindi or Punjabi, with fluency in both languages highly desirable, and will support engagement with relevant communities and, where appropriate, review or translation of research materials. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: Completion of a PhD in a relevant discipline, such as public health, psychology, health sciences, ageing, dementia, social science, health services research or a related field. Demonstrated experience undertaking research, with the capacity to independently manage defined research activities and contribute to study design, data collection, analysis and interpretation in collaboration with senior researchers. Demonstrated experience in qualitative research, including data collection, analysis and interpretation, and proficiency in qualitative research software such as NVivo. Experience undertaking quantitative or mixed-methods research will be highly regarded. Fluency in written and spoken Hindi or Punjabi. Fluency in both languages is highly desirable. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. PD-RO-Mindcare Research Officer - Bilingual 2026.pdf We’d love to stay connected! If you would like to find out more about this School, please follow us on LinkedIn: School of Humanities and Social Sciences: https://www.linkedin.com/company/89174495 Benefits 17% superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing Date: By 11:55pm Sunday 18 th October, 2026 Position Enquiries: Jo Antoniades Email: j.antoniades@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Emma Fowler, E.Fowler@latrobe.edu.au Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up to date resume; and Cover letter including response to all selection criteria Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our People At La Trobe, our people are the foundation of our success, with every role contributing to the delivery of our Strategic Plan 2025–2030 through meaningful work that makes a difference. How we work is as important as what we achieve, with our culture shaping the impact we create through everyday actions, collaboration, and shared accountability. Our sector-leading Leadership Academy develops leadership that is people first, purpose driven, intentional and embraces technology. By building the capability and confidence of all leaders, we create the conditions for individuals and teams to thrive, perform at their best and achieve shared success. Together, we foster an inclusive, respectful, and high-performing culture where excellence is recognised and celebrated. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive 