    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/en/job/571115/senior-advisor-research-governance-assurance": {
      "title": "Senior Advisor, Research Governance & Assurance",
      "description": "Senior Advisor, Research Governance & Assurance Job No.: 571115 Work type: Continuing Full Time Continuing Position based at Bundoora Campus Salary range $106,472 - $117,127 plus 17% superannuation About the position The Ethics, Integrity and Biosafety (EIB) Team of the Research Office at La Trobe University provides holistic ethics, integrity and biosafety advice, support and service to researchers and to Committees. The Senior Advisor, Research Governance and Assurance will facilitate excellent research at La Trobe University by working with stakeholders across the university to develop, implement and manage governance structures to support the effective management of risk and compliance with industry standards and regulatory schemes. The position: Provides research governance advisory services, serving as the primary liaison for the University's research partners and internal stakeholders on matters relating to research ethics and compliance requirements. In conjunction with the Clinical Trials Platform, supports clinical trials governance by providing specialist advice and coordination to researchers undertaking clinical trials, ensuring compliance with applicable regulatory and governance frameworks. Provides research quality assurance by holding primary responsibility for the University's Risk-Based Monitoring (RBM) program and internal research audit activities. Develop and deliver RBM and internal research audit reports outlining the University's compliance status, key risk trends, and open/unresolved risks, ensuring timely reporting to relevant risk committees to support institutional oversight and decision-making. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: A relevant tertiary qualification and experience in a relevant field such as research governance and ethics, compliance, tertiary education management, or health, medical or clinical research. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with an emphasis on the ability to evaluate, analyse and communicate information clearly to a range of audience. In-depth knowledge of relevant research governance frameworks and regulatory requirements, including the Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research, the National Statement on Ethical Conduct in Human Research, ICH Good Clinical Practice, the National Clinical Trials Governance Framework, the Therapeutics Goods Act 1989 and the Gene Technology Act. Demonstrated experience providing high-level advisory services on research ethics and compliance requirements to researchers and/or external research partners, including the ability to interpret and translate complex regulatory requirements into practical guidance Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. PD - Senior Advisor Research Governance and Assurance.pdf Benefits 17% employer contributed superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing date: By 11:55pm on Tuesday 17 th November 2026 Position Enquiries: Mark Li, Senior Manager, Ethics Integrity & Biosafety Email: Mark.Li@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: A cover letter outlining your relevant skills and experience required for the position and, An up-to-date resume. Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Advertised: 27/10/2026 Closing Date: 17/11/2026 Back to search results Apply now"
    },
    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/research-officer-melbourne-bundoora-vic-australia-26011d55-ed77-44ca-be60-da9cc3bc1c38": {
      "title": "Research Officer",
      "description": "Research Officer - Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit  La Trobe University My Profile Kiosk mode Research Officer 571181 Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Fixed Term Closing on: 8 Dec 2026 Part-Time, Fixed Term position with possibility for extension Melbourne (Bundoora) Classification: Level A - Base salary from $84,205 -$112,802 + 17% superannuation About the position This position contributes to the Australian Research Council Linkage Project, “An Evidence-Based Strategy to Advance Modular Hempcrete Panels in Australia”. The Researcher will work with La Trobe University Chief Investigators and the three project partners (the Australian Hemp Council, the Warner Research Institute and Southern Hemp) to assess the potential of modular hempcrete panels as an affordable, low-carbon construction solution and their contribution to regional development. The role will bring together quantitative and qualitative evidence to examine the opportunities, constraints, investment needs and regulatory considerations involved in developing the Australian hempcrete panel industry. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: Completion of a relevant Master’s degree or PhD, or be close to submission, in a field such as environmental science, agricultural or resource economics, regional development, ecology, public policy, supply-chain management or a related discipline. Evidence of experience in research and evaluation and the ability to work effectively under limited supervision or independently. A record of contribution to publications, conference papers and/or reports, or professional or technical contributions which provide evidence of research potential. Experience in the analysis and modelling of data, including the capacity to integrate data from a range of sources and of uneven quality. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Level A Research Only Research Officer PD.pdf We’d love to stay connected! If you would like to find out more about this School, please follow us on LinkedIn: La Trobe Business School: https://www.linkedin.com/company/28386791 Benefits 17% superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing Date: By 11:55pm on Tuesday 8th December 2026 Position Enquiries: David Fleming Munoz, Professor Agricultural and Resource Economics Email: D.FlemingMunoz@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up to date resume; Cover letter, and Responses to selection criteria Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our People At La Trobe, our people are the foundation of our success, with every role contributing to the delivery of our Strategic Plan 2025–2030 through meaningful work that makes a difference. How we work is as important as what we achieve, with our culture shaping the impact we create through everyday actions, collaboration, and shared accountability. Our sector-leading Leadership Academy develops leadership that is people first, purpose driven, intentional and embraces technology. By building the capability and confidence of all leaders, we create the conditions for individuals and teams to thrive, perform at their best and achieve shared success. Together, we foster an inclusive, respectful, and high-performing culture where excellence is recognised and celebrated. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005 .  If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a234f2d2 Last Name (required) 2e1788d4 Email (required) 39479abd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Senior Lecturer, Speech Pathology (TF) Bendigo, VIC Academic : Community & Clinical Health, Academic : Health Services, Academic : Psychology, Counselling & Therapy, Academic : Public Health, Academic : Teaching Focused Shape the next generation of speech pathology professionals through innovative teaching. Manager, Academic Policy and Governance Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Educational Services, Professional: Governance Shape and strengthen La Trobe University’s academic policy framework, ensuring it remains aligned with strategic priorities, governance and regulatory requirements. Statewide Co-ordinator - Families where a Parent has a Mental Illness Program Bouverie Centre (Brunswick), Victoria Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Community Engagement, Professional: Education and Training, Professional: Project Management Lead statewide delivery of the Families where a Parent has a Mental Illness Program, strengthening family-inclusive mental health practice, strategic partnerships and outcomes for children, parents and families across Victoria. Register for job alerts Job Alert 28e25949 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance Academic : Research Academic : Social Inquiry Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance Academic : Research Academic : Social Inquiry Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Employment Type Fixed Term Fixed Term Locations Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia First Name (required) 414ffc2a Last Name (required) b98235fd Email (required) 184da500 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X Youtube LinkedIn Tiktok Instagram © 2026 La Trobe University | All rights reserved | TEQSA PRV12132 - Australian University | CRICOS Provider 00115M Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright and disclaimer Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
