    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/manager-academic-policy-and-governance-melbourne-bundoora-vic-australia": {
      "title": "Manager, Academic Policy and Governance",
      "description": "Manager, Academic Policy and Governance - Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit  La Trobe University My Profile Kiosk mode Manager, Academic Policy and Governance 571136 Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Continuing Closing on: 29 Nov 2026 Shape the strategic direction & continuous improvement of the academic policy function Provide strategic academic policy advice & reporting to senior leaders and governance bodies Full Time / Continuing / Melbourne (Bundoora) Campus / HEO9 About the position The Manager, Academic Policy and Governance leads the development, management and continuous improvement of La Trobe University’s academic policy framework, ensuring policies remain current, effective and aligned with strategic, governance and regulatory requirements. Working across the University, the role provides authoritative advice, leads complex policy reform and supports the effective implementation and understanding of academic policy. Duties at this level: Lead and manage the University’s academic policy portfolio, including the policy roadmap, review schedule, prioritisation of new and revised policies, and oversight of policy status, interdependencies and risks. Lead the end-to-end development and review of academic policies, procedures, standards and related instruments, ensuring they are evidence-based, accessible and aligned with legislation, the Higher Education Standards Framework and University strategy. Assess the broader implications of proposed policy changes across academic quality, regulatory compliance, operations, systems and data, resourcing, equity, risk, communications and change. Lead scheduled and post-implementation policy reviews, identifying and recommending corrective actions, amendments and improvements where required. Provide authoritative strategic advice on academic policy, regulatory and governance matters to senior leaders, Schools, Divisions and University governance bodies, translating complex requirements into clear, practical recommendations. Skills and knowledge: A relevant degree with extensive experience and management expertise, postgraduate qualifications with relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of knowledge, training and experience. Demonstrated expertise in managing the end-to-end policy lifecycle, including development, consultation, governance, implementation, evaluation and review. Strong knowledge of the Australian higher education regulatory and quality environment, including the Higher Education Standards Framework, with the ability to translate regulatory requirements into practical policy and advice. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to clearly communicate complex policy, regulatory and governance matters and produce high-quality policies, briefs, reports and guidance materials. Please refer to the position description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. How to apply Closing date: Sunday 29th November, 2026 at 11:55pm Position Enquiries: Tim Smith, Associate Director, Academic Strategy and Operations, DVC Academic, Email: Tim.Smith@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Vicki Stavrou, Senior Talent Partner, Strategy and Senior Appointments Email: v.stavrou@latrobe.edu.au Position Description below: PD-Manager Academic Policy and Governance.pdf Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: Cover letter and An up-to-date resume *Please note, only candidates who possess the full rights to work in Australia will be eligible for consideration* Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005 .  If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 2a40c037 Last Name (required) f71f8409 Email (required) 16b4e337 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Research Officer Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance, Academic : Research , Academic : Social Inquiry, Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Support research into sustainable hempcrete panels and their potential for regional development. Senior Lecturer, Speech Pathology (TF) Bendigo, VIC Academic : Community & Clinical Health, Academic : Health Services, Academic : Psychology, Counselling & Therapy, Academic : Public Health, Academic : Teaching Focused Shape the next generation of speech pathology professionals through innovative teaching. Statewide Co-ordinator - Families where a Parent has a Mental Illness Program Bouverie Centre (Brunswick), Victoria Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Community Engagement, Professional: Education and Training, Professional: Project Management Lead statewide delivery of the Families where a Parent has a Mental Illness Program, strengthening family-inclusive mental health practice, strategic partnerships and outcomes for children, parents and families across Victoria. Register for job alerts Job Alert b243fbd8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Classification Level - Professional: HEO9 Professional: Educational Services Professional: Governance Classification Level - Professional: HEO9 Professional: Educational Services Professional: Governance Employment Type Continuing Continuing Locations Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia First Name (required) 2f3ce82b Last Name (required) c99318a4 Email (required) 52414df7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X Youtube LinkedIn Tiktok Instagram © 2026 La Trobe University | All rights reserved | TEQSA PRV12132 - Australian University | CRICOS Provider 00115M Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright and disclaimer Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
