    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/research-officer-melbourne-bundoora-vic-australia": {
      "title": "Research Officer",
      "description": "Research Officer - Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit  La Trobe University My Profile Kiosk mode Research Officer 571216 Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Fixed Term Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 Full-Time, Fixed Term position Melbourne (Bundoora) Classification: HEO5 - Base salary from $84,084 + 17% superannuation Hybrid work model support About the position La Trobe University is seeking a Research Officer to support a research program involving specialized flow cytometry experiments using human samples. The position will be based across La Trobe University and the flow cytometry facility at WEHI in Parkville. The successful applicant will work with the Senior Research Fellow, research staff, students and collaborators to conduct, optimize, analyses and document flow cytometry experiments. This role would suit an early-career researcher who is technically capable, collaborative and able to work with a degree of independence. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: Evidence of experience in research and evaluation and the ability to work effectively under limited supervision or independently. A record of contribution to publications, conference papers and/or reports, or professional or technical contributions which provide evidence of research potential. Experience in the analysis and modelling of data, including the capacity to integrate data from a range of sources and of uneven quality. Effective oral and written communication skills, including the ability to interact effectively with people from a diverse range of backgrounds. Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Level A Research Officer PD.pdf Benefits 17% superannuation Private Health Insurance discount Plus, many more, click HERE How to apply Closing Date: By 11:55pm on Sunday 15th November 2026 Position Enquiries: Sarah Annesley, Senior Research Fellow Email: S.Annesley@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: Emma Fowler, Talent Acquisition Operations Officer, E.Fowler@latrobe.edu.au Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up to date resume; and Cover letter addressing essential criteria and skills required for the role Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our People At La Trobe, our people are the foundation of our success, with every role contributing to the delivery of our Strategic Plan 2025–2030 through meaningful work that makes a difference. How we work is as important as what we achieve, with our culture shaping the impact we create through everyday actions, collaboration, and shared accountability. Our sector-leading Leadership Academy develops leadership that is people first, purpose driven, intentional and embraces technology. By building the capability and confidence of all leaders, we create the conditions for individuals and teams to thrive, perform at their best and achieve shared success. Together, we foster an inclusive, respectful, and high-performing culture where excellence is recognised and celebrated. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005 .  If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) f41a918c Last Name (required) 408253a9 Email (required) 7e773da0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Research Officer Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance, Academic : Research , Academic : Social Inquiry, Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Support research into sustainable hempcrete panels and their potential for regional development. Senior Lecturer, Speech Pathology (TF) Bendigo, VIC Academic : Community & Clinical Health, Academic : Health Services, Academic : Psychology, Counselling & Therapy, Academic : Public Health, Academic : Teaching Focused Shape the next generation of speech pathology professionals through innovative teaching. Manager, Academic Policy and Governance Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Educational Services, Professional: Governance Shape and strengthen La Trobe University’s academic policy framework, ensuring it remains aligned with strategic priorities, governance and regulatory requirements. Register for job alerts Job Alert d265543b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic : Education Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Academic : Education Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Employment Type Fixed Term Fixed Term Locations Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia First Name (required) b7a3032f Last Name (required) e98bf61b Email (required) c134493d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X Youtube LinkedIn Tiktok Instagram © 2026 La Trobe University | All rights reserved | TEQSA PRV12132 - Australian University | CRICOS Provider 00115M Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright and disclaimer Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
