    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-anatomy-tf-melbourne-bundoora-vic-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Anatomy (TF)",
      "description": "Lecturer - Anatomy (TF) - Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit  La Trobe University My Profile Kiosk mode Lecturer - Anatomy (TF) 571179 Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Continuing Closing on: 18 Nov 2026 Full-time (or part-time available), continuing Level B Teaching-Focused Position La Trobe Melbourne (Bundoora) Campus Location About the Role In this role, you will coordinate and teach across multiple anatomy subjects, supporting cohesive curriculum delivery and high-quality student learning. You may also contribute to physiology teaching as required. Your teaching will support applied learning relevant to allied health practice and align with professional standards and accreditation requirements. You will contribute to excellence in learning and teaching through evidence-based and scholarly practice, and take an active role in subject and course design, delivery, and review. The role includes mentoring sessional and early-career staff, supporting continuous improvement, and contributing to the operational and strategic development of the Anatomy discipline. Skills and knowledge required for the position A PhD or equivalent accreditation/standing recognised by the University and profession as appropriate to the discipline of Anatomy or a closely aligned field. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching and subject coordination across face-to-face, blended and/or online modes, evidenced by strong student feedback, peer review, teaching awards, or other credible indicators of teaching quality. Demonstrated ability to design, deliver and evaluate engaging, evidence-informed and clinically relevant curriculum , including contributions to subject and/or course redevelopment. Demonstrated engagement with the Scholarship of Teaching and Learning (SoTL) and/or clinical research , with a clear trajectory of developing expertise in these areas. Please view the position description for all other duties and essential skills/requirements required for the position. Essential Requirements: To hold this La Trobe University position the occupant must: hold, or be willing to undertake and pass, a Victorian Working With Children Check; AND take personal accountability to comply with all University policies, procedures and legislative or regulatory obligations; including but not limited to TEQSA and the Higher Education Threshold Standards. Position Description: Level B_PD_TF_Anatomy.docx Apply now and make an impact! How to apply Closing date: Wednesday the 18th of November 2026 Position enquiries: Steve Petrovski, HOD Microbiology, Anatomy, Physiology and Pharmacology Email: steve.petrovski@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment enquiries: Madeleine Parker, Talent Acquisition Consultant Email: m.parker@latrobe.edu.au Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; and A cover letter; and A separate document addressing your suitability for the position, addressing each essential and desirable bullet point in the position description under \"Skills and knowledge required for the position\". Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Why La Trobe: Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future Please scroll down to apply. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005.  If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation liberty or autonomy. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) e984c3d4 Last Name (required) e44cb7c6 Email (required) 796cccda Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Research Officer Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance, Academic : Research , Academic : Social Inquiry, Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Support research into sustainable hempcrete panels and their potential for regional development. Senior Lecturer, Speech Pathology (TF) Bendigo, VIC Academic : Community & Clinical Health, Academic : Health Services, Academic : Psychology, Counselling & Therapy, Academic : Public Health, Academic : Teaching Focused Shape the next generation of speech pathology professionals through innovative teaching. Manager, Academic Policy and Governance Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Educational Services, Professional: Governance Shape and strengthen La Trobe University’s academic policy framework, ensuring it remain