    "https://jobs.latrobe.edu.au/jobs/director-summer-disability-research-centre-campus-independent-vic-australia": {
      "title": "Director, Summer Disability Research Centre",
      "description": "Director, Summer Disability Research Centre - Campus Independent, VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit  La Trobe University My Profile Kiosk mode Director, Summer Disability Research Centre 569921 Campus Independent, VIC Fixed Term Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 Fixed Term (4 years), Full-Time Professor Classification Level E Base salary from ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR/ PROFESSOR LEVEL E + 17% superannuation About the position La Trobe University is seeking an outstanding research leader to take on the role of Director, The Summer Disability Research Centre, established through a strategic partnership between The Summer Foundation and the School of Psychology and Public Health at La Trobe University. This unique position is funded by The Summer Foundation and provides the opportunity to lead a nationally significant program of disability research. This is a rare opportunity to lead a purpose-driven research centre focused on generating evidence that improves housing, support and living outcomes for people with disability with high support needs. The Director will provide strategic leadership for the Centre's research agenda, secure competitive and philanthropic funding, build a high-performing, multidisciplinary research team, and ensure that research findings are translated into policy, practice, and systems change. Working at the intersection of research, policy, innovation and practice, the role draws on The Summer Foundation's extensive sector expertise, lived experience partnerships and national policy influence to generate rigorous evidence that informs policy reform, service innovation and systems change for people with disability with high support needs. The Director will foster a collaborative, inclusive research culture grounded in co-design and participatory research, ensuring people with lived experience of disability are central to the Centre’s work. Reporting to the Dean, School of Psychology and Public Health, the role contributes to the School’s research strategy, performance and external engagement at a national and international level. Skills and Experience To be considered for this position, you will have: A PhD or equivalent qualification in a relevant discipline such as psychology, public health, social sciences, rehabilitation or disability studies A distinguished record of research achievement at Associate Professor/Professor level or equivalent , including high-impact publications, competitive research funding and demonstrated research impact A strong track record of translating research into policy, practice or systems change, particularly within the disability, housing or health sectors Demonstrated experience providing strategic leadership to a research centre or large research program, including staff leadership and performance management Proven success in building and sustaining collaborative partnerships with government agencies, disability organisations, service providers and people with lived experience A deep understanding of issues affecting people with disability and a commitment to inclusive, accessible and ethical research practices Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder engagement skills Capacity to contribute to research supervision, HDR supervision and research capability development. A demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion, including creating respectful and accessible working environments Please refer to the Position Description for other duties, skills and experience required for this position. Benefits 17% employer contributed superannuation On site child care facilities Flexible work arrangements Discounts for staff and their family members to study a range of La Trobe courses How to apply Position Enquiries: Bircan Erbas Associate Dean Research & Industry Engagement, B.erbas@latrobe.edu.au Recruitment Enquiries: recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Only candidates with Full Working Rights in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit an online application ONLY and include the following documents: An up-to-date resume; and cover letter Response to Essential criteria Please scroll down to apply. Director Summer Foundation PD...docx We’d love to stay connected! If you would like to find out more about this School, please follow us on LinkedIn: School of Psychology and Public Health https://www.linkedin.com/company/school-of-psychology-and-public-health-la-trobe-university/ Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We welcome and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Our commitment to diversity and inclusion La Trobe University is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workforce. We take an intersectional approach by actively supporting and encouraging people of all backgrounds and abilities to submit an application and aim to ensure that the recruitment and employee experience is as accessible and inclusive as possible. Flexibility in interview format will be offered to shortlisted candidates. Our commitment to safety All La Trobe University employees are bound by the Working with Children Act 2005. If you are successful, you will be required to hold a valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check prior to commencement. National Code on Gender Based Violence in Higher Education La Trobe University is committed to upholding the National Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence (GBV Code). This aligns with our mission to create safe and respectful communities. Candidates will be asked during the recruitment process to declare whether they have ever been investigated for, or found to have engaged in, gender-based violence in previous employment and/or in legal proceedings and provide relevant information to assist in determining suitability. Gender-based violence means any form of physical or non-physical violence, harassment, abuse or threats based on gender, that results in, or is likely to result in harm, coercion, control, fear or deprivation of liberty or autonomy. Why La Trobe Develop your career at an innovative, global university where you’ll collaborate with community and industry to create impact. Enjoy working on our inspiring and stunning campuses – the perfect hub for industry, students and academics. Help transform the lives of students, partners and communities now and in the future. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 5989a49a Last Name (required) a88fbc8d Email (required) 79a03a69 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Research Officer Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance, Academic : Research , Academic : Social Inquiry, Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Support research into sustainable hempcrete panels and their potential for regional development. Senior Lecturer, Speech Pathology (TF) Bendigo, VIC Academic : Community & Clinical Health, Academic : Health Services, Academic : Psychology, Counselling & Therapy, Academic : Public Health, Academic : Teaching Focused Shape the next generation of speech pathology professionals through innovative teaching. Manager, Academic Policy and Governance Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Educational Services, Professional: Governance Shape and strengthen La Trobe University’s academic policy framework, ensuring it remains aligned with strategic priorities, governance and regulatory requirements. Register for job alerts Job Alert 71416888 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic : Public Health Academic : Public Health Employment Type Fixed Term Fixed Term Locations Campus Independent, VIC, Australia Campus Independent, VIC, Australia First Name (required) d0263d60 Last Name (required) cba62c70 Email (required) 54807bfb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X Youtube LinkedIn Tiktok Instagram © 2026 La Trobe University | All rights reserved | TEQSA PRV12132 - Australian University | CRICOS Provider 00115M Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright and disclaimer Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
