      "description": "Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest - Campus Independent, VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit  La Trobe University My Profile Kiosk mode Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest 544876 Campus Independent, VIC Continuing Fixed Term La Trobe University is strongly committed to providing employment opportunities to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples in all academic and professional roles and levels. Indigenous Australian candidates can register an Expression of Interest for consideration and notification of roles that may become available in the future. These details will remain on file for a period of twelve (12) months and actively matched against any suitable position that may arise during that time. Indigenous employment enquiries may be forwarded to the La Trobe Recruitment Team via email at Recruitment@latrobe.edu.au Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a8bd9c3b Last Name (required) e9639083 Email (required) 93813c84 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Research Officer Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Academic : Accounting, Data Analytics, Economics & Finance, Academic : Research , Academic : Social Inquiry, Classification Level - Academic: Level A - Research Only Support research into sustainable hempcrete panels and their potential for regional development. Senior Lecturer, Speech Pathology (TF) Bendigo, VIC Academic : Community & Clinical Health, Academic : Health Services, Academic : Psychology, Counselling & Therapy, Academic : Public Health, Academic : Teaching Focused Shape the next generation of speech pathology professionals through innovative teaching. Manager, Academic Policy and Governance Melbourne (Bundoora), VIC Classification Level - Professional: HEO9, Professional: Educational Services, Professional: Governance Shape and strengthen La Trobe University’s academic policy framework, ensuring it remains aligned with strategic pr